# Copied to .open-next/assets/_headers by scripts/cloudflare/finalize-assets.mjs.
#
# Static files (public/ and /_next/static) are answered by Workers static assets without reaching the
# Next.js server, so next.config.ts headers() never sees them — exactly as Netlify's netlify.toml
# [[headers]] rule was the only thing that reached its publish directory. These are the headers that
# rule set, verified against production before the move: HSTS and `Access-Control-Allow-Origin: *` on
# every static file (browser clients of the public API and data files depend on the latter), and the
# year-long immutable cache on content-hashed build assets.

/*
  Strict-Transport-Security: max-age=63072000
  Access-Control-Allow-Origin: *

/_next/static/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=31536000, immutable
